# Destinations the proxy refuses (POSIX extended regex, case-insensitive).
# Tinyproxy matches these against the request URL (plain HTTP) or the
# host:port of a CONNECT tunnel. They stop literal internal targets; a public
# name that resolves to a private address is not caught here (see README,
# "Security design").

# Loopback, RFC 1918, link-local and CGNAT/Tailscale address literals
^(https?://)?(localhost|127\.|0\.|10\.|169\.254\.|172\.(1[6-9]|2[0-9]|3[01])\.|192\.168\.|100\.(6[4-9]|[7-9][0-9]|1[01][0-9]|12[0-7])\.)
# IPv6 literals (loopback, ULA, link-local)
^(https?://)?\[(::1|f[cd][0-9a-f]{2}:|fe80:)
# Internal-looking names
\.(local|internal|lan|home|arpa|ts\.net)(:[0-9]+)?(/|$)
# Plain HTTP to an explicit port (only the default port 80 is allowed)
^http://[^/]+:[0-9]+
